{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Upon me, and I will bind them</b> — from the root מוסר, and the yod is absorbed with a dagesh in the root letter ע of the verb, like בטרם אצרך בבטן (before I formed you in the womb), כי אצק מים. And the meaning: and the nations will gather against them, how I will bind them through nations that will assemble against them." "<b>And I will bind them</b> — like יאסרו קשורים (they are bound in fetters)." "<b>For their two iniquities</b> — like כבחצי מענה, they lengthened for their benefit. And the reason for 'two': on account of Judah and Ephraim."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The two biblical quotations in the second example are abbreviated or fragmentary; rendered hyper-literally as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:51.801988194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}